{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Behemah</b> — these are the species that eat vegetation, whether domesticated or wild." "<b>And the living creatures of the land</b> — those that eat flesh He calls חיות (living creatures), and all of them are predators." "<b>And creeping things</b> — Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 1:24): these are low creeping things that move upon the earth, appearing as though they are being dragged. But in this passage (Genesis 1:28) it says: \"and in every living creature that creeps upon the earth,\" and it is written (Genesis 7:21): \"And all flesh that creeps upon the earth perished — in birds, in beasts, in living creatures, and in every swarming thing that swarms upon the earth,\" and it is written (Psalms 104:20): \"wherein every beast of the forest creeps.\" But the meaning of רמישה (creeping) is like the sense with samekh, from \"תרמסנה רגל\" (Isaiah 26:6) and its cognates. And concerning the living creatures and the behemah He said \"creeping upon the earth,\" but concerning the creeping things that are dragged along He said \"creeping thing of the ground\" (Genesis 1:25), because their treading is upon the ground with their entire body."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:15:06.149386948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}